{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LVZZ2rfys6woXA7ZNgMyBd","type":"tool_result","content":"11:- make validation and reporting consistent\n37:  templates/     # spec.md, roadmap.md, knowledge.md, changelog-fragment.md, doc-audit-report.md\n45:  reports/       # versionable reports + history JSONL + archive/\n65:[Omitted long matching line]\n73:- [`.pose/templates/doc-audit-report.md`](.pose/templates/doc-audit-report.md): template for editorial reviews and documentation audits.\n74:- `pose` binary: native scaffold/check/validate/report automation and MCP server.\n118:  and reports `cause: dependency` or `cause: unknown`; spec transfer also uses\n136:- **Follow-ups with disposition:** the `Final Report > Follow-ups` section is\n147:  `pose lint-spec` warns about it. Legacy items without the group are reported\n151:  evidence (free text plus structured refs `check:`, `test:`, `report:`,\n160:  `pose close` while the spec is open, and is only reported on a closed spec.\n217:pose validate [--strict|--tolerant] [--stack s] [--module path] [--report] [--json-out f] [--junit f] [--sarif f]\n218:              [--changed-from rev [--changed-to rev] | --carry] [--jobs n] [--explain] [--emit-plan f]\n275:pose stats governance [--since-days N] [--maturity-days N] [--min-sample N] [--band baseline|elevated|critical|unknown] [--report-type standard|doc-audit|unknown] [--waits] [--rework] [--outcomes] [--json]\n292:pose report --task \"...\" [--outcome pass|fail|partial|skipped|unknown] [--since <ref>] [--git-stage] [...]\n304:pose reports-housekeeping <list-stale|archive-stale|purge-archived> [--older-than N] [--dry-run|--apply]\n324:pose report-limitation --title \"...\" --kind limitation|bug|suggestion [--body \"...\"] [--submit]\n328:                                   # reports under .pose/contributions/ without leaking\n343:[Omitted long matching line]\n346:[Omitted long matching line]\n353:[Omitted long matching line]\n355:[Omitted long matching line]\n357:[Omitted long matching line]\n359:[Omitted long matching line]\n360:[Omitted long matching line]\n361:[Omitted long matching line]\n363:- `report` — generates a versionable report in `.pose/reports/` with execution metadata, minimal per-task history (`.pose/reports/history/`) and stable-field diffs.\n365:[Omitted long matching line]\n366:[Omitted long matching line]\n369:[Omitted long matching line]\n370:[Omitted long matching line]\n371:[Omitted long matching line]\n372:[Omitted long matching line]\n374:  **Removal witnesses:** a review subject path a later spec removed reads as that removal only while Git still shows it: the deleting commit on `HEAD`, read raw, with no later commit touching the path, in a clone that is not shallow. Otherwise preparation refuses and asks for `pose index`. A generation binds the change sets of `.pose/reports/history` as `recorded-change-sets`, so one published earlier reads as unbound until the next `pose index`.\n376:[Omitted long matching line]\n377:[Omitted long matching line]\n380:[Omitted long matching line]\n382:- `surface-check` / `roadmap-check` — extend the same graph with typed `delivers` refs, production entrypoints, closed validation `evidenceClass` values and provenance-bound structured results. Surface profiles require reachability plus integration/e2e; composed capabilities require integration. Roadmap criteria may reference only registered delivery refs, checks or confined manual-review reports—raw commands are rejected. MCP: `pose_surface_assurance`.\n383:[Omitted long matching line]\n385:[Omitted long matching line]\n386:[Omitted long matching line]\n390:[Omitted long matching line]\n392:[Omitted long matching line]\n394:[Omitted long matching line]\n397:[Omitted long matching line]\n398:[Omitted long matching line]\n399:[Omitted long matching line]\n401:[Omitted long matching line]\n406:[Omitted long matching line]\n411:- `history-check` — verifies every `.jsonl` under `reports/history/` is git-tracked. Without that, `recurrence-check` and `stats` diverge between machines. Strict blocks; tolerant warns.\n412:[Omitted long matching line]\n414:[Omitted long matching line]\n415:[Omitted long matching line]\n416:[Omitted long matching line]\n422:[Omitted long matching line]\n425:- `knowledge-housekeeping` / `reports-housekeeping` / `events-housekeeping` — idempotent maintenance (list/archive/purge). Mutations require `--apply`. Reports housekeeping **never touches `history/`**: the JSONL is the source of truth for `recurrence-check` and `report`'s temporal comparisons. Defaults: stale = 120d, archive purge = 365d.\n427:[Omitted long matching line]\n437:- `report-limitation` — records an engine limitation, defect, or enhancement proposal into `.pose/feedback/` with optional submission (`--submit`).\n438:- `contribute <enable|disable|status|stage|list>` — open-source contributor mode; stages sanitized reports under `.pose/contributions/` without leaking proprietary code; submission remains developer-adjudicated.\n440:[Omitted long matching line]\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 60]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"f5e77129-918b-4e7d-92dd-bb06959def39","timestamp":"2026-11-28T13:42:05.811Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"11:- make validation and reporting consistent\n37:  templates/     # spec.md, roadmap.md, knowledge.md, changelog-fragment.md, doc-audit-report.md\n45:  reports/       # versionable reports + history JSONL + archive/\n65:[Omitted long matching line]\n73:- [`.pose/templates/doc-audit-report.md`](.pose/templates/doc-audit-report.md): template for editorial reviews and documentation audits.\n74:- `pose` binary: native scaffold/check/validate/report automation and MCP server.\n118:  and reports `cause: dependency` or `cause: unknown`; spec transfer also uses\n136:- **Follow-ups with disposition:** the `Final Report > Follow-ups` section is\n147:  `pose lint-spec` warns about it. Legacy items without the group are reported\n151:  evidence (free text plus structured refs `check:`, `test:`, `report:`,\n160:  `pose close` while the spec is open, and is only reported on a closed spec.\n217:pose validate [--strict|--tolerant] [--stack s] [--module path] [--report] [--json-out f] [--junit f] [--sarif f]\n218:              [--changed-from rev [--changed-to rev] | --carry] [--jobs n] [--explain] [--emit-plan f]\n275:pose stats governance [--since-days N] [--maturity-days N] [--min-sample N] [--band baseline|elevated|critical|unknown] [--report-type standard|doc-audit|unknown] [--waits] [--rework] [--outcomes] [--json]\n292:pose report --task \"...\" [--outcome pass|fail|partial|skipped|unknown] [--since <ref>] [--git-stage] [...]\n304:pose reports-housekeeping <list-stale|archive-stale|purge-archived> [--older-than N] [--dry-run|--apply]\n324:pose report-limitation --title \"...\" --kind limitation|bug|suggestion [--body \"...\"] [--submit]\n328:                                   # reports under .pose/contributions/ without leaking\n343:[Omitted long matching line]\n346:[Omitted long matching line]\n353:[Omitted long matching line]\n355:[Omitted long matching line]\n357:[Omitted long matching line]\n359:[Omitted long matching line]\n360:[Omitted long matching line]\n361:[Omitted long matching line]\n363:- `report` — generates a versionable report in `.pose/reports/` with execution metadata, minimal per-task history (`.pose/reports/history/`) and stable-field diffs.\n365:[Omitted long matching line]\n366:[Omitted long matching line]\n369:[Omitted long matching line]\n370:[Omitted long matching line]\n371:[Omitted long matching line]\n372:[Omitted long matching line]\n374:  **Removal witnesses:** a review subject path a later spec removed reads as that removal only while Git still shows it: the deleting commit on `HEAD`, read raw, with no later commit touching the path, in a clone that is not shallow. Otherwise preparation refuses and asks for `pose index`. A generation binds the change sets of `.pose/reports/history` as `recorded-change-sets`, so one published earlier reads as unbound until the next `pose index`.\n376:[Omitted long matching line]\n377:[Omitted long matching line]\n380:[Omitted long matching line]\n382:- `surface-check` / `roadmap-check` — extend the same graph with typed `delivers` refs, production entrypoints, closed validation `evidenceClass` values and provenance-bound structured results. Surface profiles require reachability plus integration/e2e; composed capabilities require integration. Roadmap criteria may reference only registered delivery refs, checks or confined manual-review reports—raw commands are rejected. MCP: `pose_surface_assurance`.\n383:[Omitted long matching line]\n385:[Omitted long matching line]\n386:[Omitted long matching line]\n390:[Omitted long matching line]\n392:[Omitted long matching line]\n394:[Omitted long matching line]\n397:[Omitted long matching line]\n398:[Omitted long matching line]\n399:[Omitted long matching line]\n401:[Omitted long matching line]\n406:[Omitted long matching line]\n411:- `history-check` — verifies every `.jsonl` under `reports/history/` is git-tracked. Without that, `recurrence-check` and `stats` diverge between machines. Strict blocks; tolerant warns.\n412:[Omitted long matching line]\n414:[Omitted long matching line]\n415:[Omitted long matching line]\n416:[Omitted long matching line]\n422:[Omitted long matching line]\n425:- `knowledge-housekeeping` / `reports-housekeeping` / `events-housekeeping` — idempotent maintenance (list/archive/purge). Mutations require `--apply`. Reports housekeeping **never touches `history/`**: the JSONL is the source of truth for `recurrence-check` and `report`'s temporal comparisons. Defaults: stale = 120d, archive purge = 365d.\n427:[Omitted long matching line]\n437:- `report-limitation` — records an engine limitation, defect, or enhancement proposal into `.pose/feedback/` with optional submission (`--submit`).\n438:- `contribute <enable|disable|status|stage|list>` — open-source contributor mode; stages sanitized reports under `.pose/contributions/` without leaking proprietary code; submission remains developer-adjudicated.\n440:[Omitted long matching line]","numLines":60,"totalLines":97,"appliedLimit":60},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LVZZ2rfys6woXA7ZNgMyBd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
